mothershipOS: the playback I/O path (used whenever the device has no direct mmap, e.g. a plug/dmix chain) writes
with alsa-lib's mmap (snd_pcm_mmap_begin), which needs an mmap access type: with RW access it fails with EBADFD
("Unknown errno (77)") and no sound plays. A hw device let it pass. Capture's I/O path reads with snd_pcm_readi,
which needs RW access: keep that for capture.

--- a/src/audio_backends/alsa.rs
+++ b/src/audio_backends/alsa.rs
@@ -116,5 +116,8 @@
             })?;
 
-            hwp.set_access(Access::RWInterleaved)?;
+            hwp.set_access(match s.direction {
+                Direction::Output => Access::MMapInterleaved,
+                Direction::Input => Access::RWInterleaved,
+            })?;
 
             let frame_size = u32::from(s.params.channels)
